WEBVTT

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.240
Are you all right, Vice President?

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.050
Thank you very much.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.580
I'm fine.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.640
Vice President, do you want to borrow my leggings?

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.210
Leggings?

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.330
No. It's enough just that you offered.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.040
Really?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.410
Well, I have work to do, so if you'll excuse me...

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.140
"DTO"... I've seen that someplace before.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.820
Seriously?

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.930
If you've seen that before,
Shingo, it must have been in...

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.390
Yeah. In the Corrections Office.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.220
Earlier, when I was called into the corrections office,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.980
I saw it in an email on their computer!

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.590
That makes sense!

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.270
A lot of work went into their plan.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.360
They must have planning data laying around somewhere.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.930
If we can get that data from the Corrections Office's computer,

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.330
we can show it to the School Committee as proof

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.870
that we were set up.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.800
That's right!

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.450
We can have them cancel our expulsions!

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.830
But if they disposed of their paper plan,
then wouldn't they have erased their emails, too?

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.240
That's true.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.010
They wouldn't be so stupid as to save that data.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.970
Of course it wouldn't be that easy.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.470
Don't be so hasty, gentlemen.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.800
Have you forgotten something?

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.520
Yours truly is number one when it comes to computers.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.860
I don't know about <i>number one</i>,

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.280
but I know for sure you're <i>number two</i>.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.110
Never mind defecation jokes!

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.950
What yours truly is trying to say is that even if the emails are erased, he can restore them!

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:30.990
Are you serious?

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.360
If I can download and run some restoration software,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.700
it will be done simply and easily.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.460
That being said, how are we to break into the Corrections Office?

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:41.380
We have no time left!

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.630
We only have two weeks left.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.130
Because there's no time left, we should give up?

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.010
It's the opposite.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.430
There's no time left, so there's also no time to hesitate.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.890
Let's get our hands on
that DTO planning data,

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.640
and prove that we're innocent!

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.100
Indeed. That <i>is</i> another way to think of it.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.820
Well, what the hell. I'm in, too.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.320
Better to try than to
do nothing at all, huh?

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.820
Miracles are something you make with your own hands, right?

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.090
Before the chairman stamps those expulsion forms in two weeks,

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.830
we will seize that DTO data.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.380
To take back our high school lives from them!

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.460
And to get to go to that wet T-shirt cont—

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.390
Supper!

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:23.690
Count off!

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:24.080
One!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:24.420
Two!

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:24.880
Three!

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.280
Four!

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:25.590
Five!

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:27.380
All right, get your meals.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:27.840
Yes!

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:32.180
Oh, Vice President, you dropped your handkerchief.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.390
Hmm? Oh, this?

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.350
Whoops!

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:48.790
Shingo got beat black and blue for seeing a nipple.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.330
What... What will they do to me for this<i>?</i>

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.690
I can't tell the others about this.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.810
Never mind me saying anything,
that's what she has down there?

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.040
That's<i> what she has down there?! </i>

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.580
What do I do? Let's see...

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.840
I'm just saying...

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.290
There is no way in hell I'm leaving school!

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.920
She left.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:11.720
Our cheer was cut off midway, let us try it again.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.240
Kiyoshi-dono, start us off, please.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.140
No matter what happens,

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.430
we will secure that data!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.960
To take back our high
school lives from them!

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.600
And to get to go to
that wet T-shirt contest—

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.020
That's<i> what she has down there!</i>

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.600
Somehow, I do not feel that your thoughts are in order.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.020
Like, on something even raunchier than wet T-shirts?

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.030
Huh? You guys, too?

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:31.840
No, no, no!

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.740
It's just your imagination!

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.020
My mind is on one thing!

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.010
Talking about securing the data is one thing, but...

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.560
While in this room, or in solitary,

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:29.060
the door is locked from outside, and we cannot get near the Corrections Office.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.440
And even if we were able to get near it,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.860
we cannot break in while the vice president is within.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.320
The only times we are let out into the hallway are during cleaning,

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.780
lunch breaks, and to do prison labor.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.150
Also at night, to shower.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.430
In every case, there's not enough time,

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:47.540
and the vice president is
right there next to us.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.370
As of today, there will be
no more prison labor.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.580
After school, you will stay inside the prison and study, or something to that effect.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.910
I guess that means we're not allowed outside the barricade anymore.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.720
During our lunch free time,they kick us outside, and won't let us in.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.750
If we still had prison labor,

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.180
we might have been able to sneak a saw in.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:09.890
No, cutting through iron bars that thick is out of the question.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.890
Are there no avenues?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.690
Avenues, huh?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.750
When we're out in the hall, the vice president is either watching us,

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.070
or waiting in the Corrections Office.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:24.560
What does the vice president
do in the Corrections Office?

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.990
Well, um... Eat tasty food,
and do calisthenics.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:31.110
And when the vice president isn't inside the prison?

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.250
She's either in class, or in bed,

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.090
but either way, we're locked up, then.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.970
Ugh, there's no way to break in there!

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:40.630
Shh!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.260
The committee meeting just ended.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.810
They've unanimously decided to expel you all.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:51.460
Now we wait only for the chairman to affix his seal.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.790
That's all I have to report.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.250
It really is hopeless.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.820
Though, we already knew that.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:06:59.880
Damn it!

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.400
We're running out of time!

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.350
I can't think of <i>any</i> opportunity to get into the Corrections Office.

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.600
At this point,

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.850
all we can do is steal the keys from the vice president.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:12.660
By force?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.270
That's not possible.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:17.040
You think any of us could take the vice president?

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.950
There's no guarantee that even all
five of us together could take her.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.420
There's too much risk.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:27.510
We have all experienced the vice president's inordinate strength for ourselves—

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.230
So what do we do?!

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:34.810
We use the vice president's strength against her.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.170
Andre wins!

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.200
Oh! That's four in a row!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.740
Andre is just too strong!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.910
They're about to be expelled, and yet they don't have a care in the world.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:51.120
Andre-dono is triumphant!

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.870
Andre's the strongest person in school!

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:57.050
Nah, calling him the strongest in school is going too far, isn't it?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.670
There's nobody here stronger than Andre.

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.170
Sure there is!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.170
The vice president.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:07.090
The vice president does indeed seem pretty strong—

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.550
No, no! No matter how strong she is, she's still a girl.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.590
She's no match for Andre.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:12.850
I guess you're right.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.420
I can't let that pass unchallenged.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.430
Do you honestly believe I would lose to that fat pig?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.190
No, I never said that.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.690
D-Do <i>you</i> think you can beat Andre?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.410
Do I think I can win, you ask?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.280
Come, Andre!

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.960
Before Andre-dono, yours truly shall be your opponent.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.760
Don't make me laugh, Dirty Four-eyes.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.710
Do you really think you can take me on?

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.480
Indeed I do.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:45.410
I am well aware of your strength, Vice President,

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.260
but I have tempered this body in daily prison labor.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.350
Before you challenge Andre-dono,

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:53.060
try to defeat me first, please!

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.200
Ho...

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.430
It does look like you've built your body up a little.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:57.750
Very well.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.650
I'll warm up on you.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.860
Come, Dirty Four-eyes!

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.570
Everything is proceeding as planned.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.140
Use the vice president's
strength against her?

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:07.150
What do you mean?

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.410
The vice president seems quite sure of her physical strength.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.580
Ah, you mean like how she does
calisthenics in the Corrections Office?

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:15.900
Yes.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.580
Which is why we will draw the vice president in to an arm wrestling contest with us.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.200
Sun Tzu says,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.380
"Generally, in battle, use the normal force
to engage; use the extraordinary to win."

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:29.720
Is this "Son" guy the one who said he left his hairline behind to advance in the telecom business?

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.060
Who else could it be but him?

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:31.390
Yeah.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.840
Could you put it a little simpler for us?

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.140
We steal the keys from the vice president's uniform during the contest.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:40.030
While everyone but yours truly is competing with her,

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:42.650
he will take the stolen keys and
sneak into the Corrections Office.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:46.030
This is the means to get the data from the computer.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:47.320
I get it now!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.920
Let's hit her head-on,

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:51.820
while you'll go and accomplish
the objective behind her back.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.480
It is a tactic of Sun Tzu, military strategist of yore.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.490
Not that telecommunications man.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.250
So, how exactly will we get the keys away from her?

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.540
That part is easy.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:08.630
We get the keys away from the vice president by taking
her jacket from her before she starts arm wrestling.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:10.380
Kiyoshi-dono,

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.700
what are you waiting for?

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:13.180
Go on.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.260
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.860
Vice President, may I hold your jacket for you?

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.230
I'm fine like this.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:20.710
Huh?

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.610
Yes, but... I think it would be
easier for you if you took it off.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.380
He is right!

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:27.610
No need. Let's get started, already.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.900
That crap-spraying four-eyes!

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.100
Easy part my foot.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:31.320
It's completely falling apart.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.930
I guess the jacket plan is a no-go.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.180
Okay then...

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.700
Ready...

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.490
Go!

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.000
Hmph, I can't even call that a warm up.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.300
Hurry up and move.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.530
Zounds!

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.880
Okay, Andre, let's go.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.360
One moment, please.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.420
Let me arm wrestle you too, Vice President.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:52.260
I have more backbone than Gakuto.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.840
Very well, I'll take you on.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.220
Are the two of you primed?

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:58.170
All right then...

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.800
Begin!

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.270
You are better than Dirty Four-eyes...

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.780
but looky here.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.190
What's the matter?
Is that all you've got?

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:08.730
I'm going to end this now.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.410
Her nipple...!

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.160
Her... nip... ple...!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.850
Are you all right, Vice President?!

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.330
What kind of broken-down table is this?!

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.000
We will go and retrieve a
replacement table right away!

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.340
All right. Now, who's next?

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:29.000
Shingo?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.020
Hold on, please!

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.090
You haven't finished me off yet.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.600
Don't be ridiculous.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.300
I beat you hands down.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.920
No, the table broke, so
it's still up in the air!

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.640
Contend with me all you like, it will still end the same.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.180
You can't beat me.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.110
Keep it up, Kiyoshi-dono.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.150
Buy me as much time as you can.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:49.690
Assuming you get into
the Corrections Office,

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:52.420
if the DTO data has been erased,

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.400
you'll have to recover it, right?

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.280
It may look as though it has been erased,

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.830
but it still exists as seemingly inaccessible data on the computer's hard drive.

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:04.790
If I can just download and run the restoration software, it will be done simply and easily.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:08.650
You say it's simple, but we don't know how to do it, so we couldn't.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:09.800
That's right.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.460
Which means that going into the Corrections Office...

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.720
...is a job that must fall onto yours truly.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:18.570
And easy though it may be,
it will still require some time.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.970
To that end, I need you to distract the vice president for as long as you can.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:26.360
How long will we have
to keep her busy for?

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:30.040
Hmm, at the very least, I need ten minutes.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:30.860
Ten minutes, huh?

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.300
That's a little bit more
than two minutes each.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:36.580
Considering how strong the vice president is, that will be tough.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.190
But what choice do we have?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:41.140
I'm not satisfied!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:42.720
Please let me try again!

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.160
You don't give up, do you?

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.720
Okay, fine. A rematch for the loser.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:47.250
Come!

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:48.830
Thank you very much!

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:55.050
All right! From here,
it's a race against time!

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:57.290
I'm definitely going to tie her up!

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:00.390
Even if I have to sacrifice my arm to do it!

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:03.100
Kiyoshi sure is fired the hell up.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:05.090
We might not even get our turns.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.350
He looks like he's can do it by himself.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.940
Ready...

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:09.640
Go!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.570
Hey, what's wrong?

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:16.530
I'm only using 30% of my strength.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.650
That's 30%?!

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.850
I'm starting to grow tired of this.

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:24.200
How about I finish this with 40% of my strength?

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.000
Kiyoshi-kun, hang in there!

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.120
There, you see?

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.330
Not yet. I can last longer than this.

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.860
My expulsion is riding on this!

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:36.400
Even if it breaks my arm,

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:37.840
I can't afford to lose yet—

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:39.430
Her...

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:40.590
nipple...?

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:41.840
It's gone...

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:43.620
There it is again!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.010
It's gone...

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.270
